Enable timers after install:
  systemctl --user daemon-reload
  systemctl --user enable --now homelab-backup.timer wallpaper-update.timer

Spotify Soloist (one-time, before enabling the service):
  # API key from developer.spotify.com/dashboard/soloist — install.sh
  # already prompted for and stored it (see .secrets) if it was missing.
  soloist --pair --device-name "$(hostname) (soloist)" \
    --api-key "$(secret-tool lookup service spotify-soloist key api-key)"
  # then, in the Spotify app on the same network: device picker -> select it -> play something

  systemctl --user daemon-reload
  systemctl --user enable --now spotify-soloist.service

Spotify search: needs a separate Developer app (Client ID + Secret, no
redirect URI) at developer.spotify.com/dashboard — install.sh prompts for
these too (see eww/.secrets).
